SUMMARY:Patient 101: Finding\, Evaluating\, and Using Health Information to Help Make Informed Decisions
DESCRIPTION:Curious about using the Internet and AI tools like ChatGPT for 
 health questions? This interactive session with health literacy librarians 
 from UNC-Chapel Hill introduces a simple “traffic light” 
 guide—what’s safe (green)\, what needs caution (yellow)\, and what to 
 avoid (red). Learn how to use the Internet and AI to understand medical 
 information\, prepare for appointments\, and advocate for your 
 health—without replacing professional care. Registration is appreciated 
 but not required. Those who register will receive a reminder two days 
 before the program.
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Raivynn Smith":MAILTO:raivynnsmith@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Digital/Tech Literacy, Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-17473103
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17473103
END:VEVENT
