SUMMARY:Drop-in Tech Support
DESCRIPTION:Drop-in for one-on-one technical support with library staff. A 
 chance to troubleshoot common device problems and learn basic computer\, 
 tablet\, or smartphone skills. This series will take place on the second 
 Wednesday of each month. \n\nWho should attend: Anyone with questions 
 about technology. People who want to improve their tech skills. Those who 
 want hands-on help or troubleshooting with their device. \n\nWhat we can 
 help with:  \n\n\n	\n	Using library e-resources (Libby\, Hoopla\, Consumer 
 Reports\, etc) \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Setting up an email or online account 
 \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Filling out an online form \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Setting up your 
 device \n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Installing or using apps \n	\n\n\nWhat to bring: Your 
 device (laptop\, tablet\, or smartphone)\, chargers\, and any relevant 
 passwords. \n\nPlease note that registration is required to ensure 
 dedicated technical assistance with library staff. We cannot help with 
 resume creation. Additionally\, we cannot offer medical\, financial\, or 
 legal advice. If you need in-depth assistance with job seeking\, we can 
 refer you to the library's Business Services. \n\nFor more information\, 
 please contact Anne Wells at awells@dconc.gov
