SUMMARY:Pour Decisions: Imagine a Day Without Water Glass Etching
DESCRIPTION:Join us and our friends from City of Durham Water Management on 
 Thursday\, October 15th from 4-5:30pm to create your very own custom etched 
 pint glass while learning together about the impact of water and our usage 
 of it! October 15th is Imagine a Day Without Water\, where we learn about 
 how important this essential\, renewable resource is to so much of 
 everything around us. Use our stencils and etching cream to design 
 personalized pint glass. We will provide one (1) pint glass per registrant. 
 You may bring one (1) other piece of glassware yourself if you'd like to 
 etch a different item. The glassware must be completely uncoated and no 
 other materials besides glass. (Number of items limited for the glass 
 etching materials we have\, sink usage\, space\, and time alloted. Thank 
 you for understanding!)\n\nThis program is held on Thursday\, October 15th 
 from 4-5:30pm in the MakerLab on  first floor  at Main Library. 
 Registration is required\; materials are limited. For adults.\n\nIf you 
 have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us 
 at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least 3 
 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible.
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Arts & Crafts, High & Low Sensory Stimulation, Maker, STEAM
