DTSTART:20261019T163000Z
DTEND:20261019T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
SUMMARY:Computer Classes: Excel 101
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a class that covers excel basics. This class is 
 intended for new users of Microsoft Excel\, a spreadsheet program. In this 
 class\, we will briefly cover the different parts of a spreadsheet and 
 accompanying toolbars. You will learn how to insert and format text in 
 cells\, how to insert and format columns and rows\, how to sort data\, how 
 to perform basic math functions\, and how to save and print.\n\nA more 
 advanced class\, Excel 102\, will be offered in Spring 2027. \n\nThis class 
 is a part of a series of computer classes. See the schedule 
 below:\n\nMonday\, September 28: AI Basics\nMonday\, October 12: Drop-In 
 Tech Help\nMonday\, October 19: Excel 101 \nMonday\, October 26: Drop-in 
 Tech Help\nMonday\, November 2: Troubleshoot Your Tech\nMonday\, November 
 9: Drop-in Tech Help\nMonday\, November 16: Organize Your Photos\, Files\, 
 & More
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Raivynn Smith":MAILTO:raivynnsmith@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Classes & Lectures, Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
