BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261020T220000Z
DTEND:20261020T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261020T000000Z
SUMMARY:On Teaching Thi Bui's The Best We Could Do
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this discussion guided by Duke Professors 
 Marguerite Nguyen and Susan Thananopavarn about why they love to teach Thi 
 Bui’s graphic memoir The Best We Could Do.\n\nThi Bui’s beautiful 
 graphic memoir tells her family’s story in a way that takes us through 
 war\, colonialism\, and a harrowing escape from Vietnam by boat.  It also 
 reckons with the complexity of families: what do we carry with us from our 
 past\, and what do we choose to pass onto our children?  I love to teach 
 this book because it grapples with questions we can all understand\, while 
 telling a history that often goes untaught in schools. - Prof. Susan 
 Thananopavarn\n\nFree copies of the book WILL BE available at Letters 
 Community Bookshop\, 116 W Main St.\, Durham\, for the first 15 people who 
 request one. (Please take just one book!) Watch here for updates for book 
 availability.\n\nOpen to all. Come prepared to discuss why you love (or 
 don't) this book.\n\nNOTE: WHILE THIS PROGRAM WILL BE HELD IN THE MAIN 
 CHILDREN'S PROGRAMMING ROOM AT THE DURHAM COUNTY MAIN LIBRARY\, THE BOOK IS 
 MOST APPROPRIATE FOR OLDER TEENS AND ADULTS.\n\nRegistration required at 
 the DCL event page. The link will be provided here when available.\n\n 
 \n\nBooks We Love to Teach is co-sponsored by Letters Community Bookshop. 
 It is part of “Forum @ the Library” - a monthly series featuring Duke 
 faculty sharing their work in an interactive format\, hosted by the Durham 
 County Library (DCL) in partnership with the Forum for Scholars and Publics 
 at the Franklin Humanities Institute.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Music
UID:LibCal-14288-16625686
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16625686
END:VEVENT
