SUMMARY:Real Talk!!! Community Conversation about Health
DESCRIPTION:Real Talk: Community Conversation About Health is a 
 community-centered discussion being hosted in partnership between the Duke 
 Cancer Institute Community Outreach and Engagement Office\, Duke-Durham 
 THREAD\, and the Durham County Library. The event will provide an 
 opportunity for community members to engage directly with Duke health 
 professionals in an informal setting. Topics may include clinical trials\, 
 GLP-1 medications and their impact on health and cancer\, breast cancer and 
 breast health\, nutrition\, research\, and other health questions that are 
 important to the community.
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Full Room\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larry Daniels":MAILTO:ldaniels@dconc.gov
