SUMMARY:Roxboro and Mangum Two-Way Conversion Design Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Project Description\n\nIn 2020\, the City of Durham completed 
 the Move Durham Study\, which looked at ways to improve streets in the 
 city’s core. The study recommended that Roxboro and Mangum streets be 
 converted to two-way traffic. Two-way streets can help: \n\n\n	Slow traffic 
 \n	Reduce crashes \n	Make it easier to walk and cross the street\n\n\nThese 
 improvements can be made with only a small increase in travel time for 
 drivers. \n\nThe Transportation Department started designing the two-way 
 conversion in April 2025.  \n\nDraft designs were shared with the public in 
 fall 2025 for feedback. Stop by and learn about the project or visit the 
 website https://www.durhamnc.gov/5405/Roxboro-St-and-Mangum-St-Design.
LOCATION:Main Library - Outdoors - Front Porch\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17612291
