SUMMARY:Novel Planning Deep Dive (NaNo Prep Workshop)
DESCRIPTION:To help those preparing for National Novel Writing Month 
 (November)\, Novel Planning Deep Dive will provide a walk-through of 
 fantasy author Phillip M. Locey's novel-planning process. He will cover 
 everything from the moment of first inspiration to identifying sources of 
 conflict within the plot. Even if you don't plan to participate in 
 NaNoWriMo\, if you're an author in the planning stages of your next 
 fictional work\, this workshop can deliver insight into the logical steps 
 required to flesh out a compelling narrative and make sure all the major 
 elements of a well-rounded novel are accounted for.
LOCATION:East Regional - Children's Programming Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Phillip Locey":MAILTO:plocey@dconc.gov
