URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16864401
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261029T200000Z
DTEND:20261029T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
SUMMARY:Reading Time with Ms. Chloe
DESCRIPTION:Registration Required through the included link. To schedule a 
 time\, go to: Make an Appointment - DCoL Events & Room Reservations - 
 Durham County Library\n\nDoes your child need more reading practice and 
 could benefit from more reading aloud time? Or are they just learning 
 phonics sounds and need more practice to build blending skills? Then this 
 program is for them! Schedule a 20-minute session for your child with Ms. 
 Chloe to work together with your child on reading and blending practice. 
 You’re welcome to bring your own book or I’ll pull some books that will 
 work for their range. \n\nWhile parents/ guardians don’t have to attend\, 
 they must remain on the children’s floor while their child is attending 
 their session.\n\nIf you no call/no show for two appointments in a row\, 
 all other appointments for the month will be cancelled to make room for 
 patrons who are waiting for spots.\n\nFor more information\, contact: 
 chloebullock@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Library - Children's Area\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chloe Bullock":MAILTO:chloebullock@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17619153
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17619153
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261029T200000Z
DTEND:20261029T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
SUMMARY:Laser Cut Your Own Fall Decoration
DESCRIPTION:Join the Maker   STEAM team to use the laser cutter to cut and 
 engrave an acrylic or wood fall decoration in a small group learning 
 environment with hands-on help! This month you'll be able to choose between 
 a pumpkin\, leaf\, or Dia de los Muertos outline template. We will use our 
 materials and provide materials for one acrylic or wood wall/door 
 decoration (roughly 5"x5" size) per registrant. Come ready with a design 
 idea or just curiosity\, and we will show you how you can design your 
 own.\n\nThis small-group atmosphere will help introduce you to the laser 
 cutter in a welcoming setting and show you the process of completing a 
 laser cut project to help you prepare for when you reserve the laser cutter 
 on your own in the future.\n\nRegistration is required. Participants will 
 need to sign a safety waiver when in the makerspace. (This program is open 
 to teens and adults. Teens under the age of 18 must have a guardian/parent 
 present to sign the waiver.)\n\nWe also ask that you take the online\, 
 self-paced laser cutter orientation prior to coming to the program (if you 
 haven't already) so that the orientation setup steps are 
 completed.\n\nNote: If you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:High & Low Sensory Stimulation, Innovation Lab, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-17576382
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17576382
END:VEVENT
