BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261031T160000Z
DTEND:20261031T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T000000Z
SUMMARY:A Spooktacular Tea Party
DESCRIPTION:Calling all little witches\, wizards\, ghosts\, and ghouls! 
 Join us for a frightfully fun Halloween Tea Party at the library filled 
 with spooky sips\, tasty treats\, and magical memories. Children and 
 families can enjoy a spooktacular tea party experience featuring 
 Halloween-inspired snacks and a craft. Put on your favorite costume\, grab 
 your teacup\, and get ready for an afternoon of Halloween fun that is sure 
 to be fang-tastic!\n\nRegistration is recommended. All ages are 
 welcome.\n\nRegistration is required! Please register everyone who will be 
 attending this event! \n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at cromero@dconc.gov or 
 againes@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least three (3) 
 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible!\n\nThis program will be held on October 31\, 
 2026\, at 12:00 p.m. at North Regional Library. The address is 221 Milton 
 Rd. Durham\, NC 27712.
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17317983
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17317983
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261031T160000Z
DTEND:20261031T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T000000Z
SUMMARY:Duke Ballet & Books
DESCRIPTION:Duke Ballet & Books is a group of Duke University student 
 volunteers who run free arts and literacy programming for 6-9 year 
 olds.\n\nThere are two parts to every Ballet & Books session:\n\n1. 
 45-minute ballet class where students learn choreography to perform at an 
 end-of-semester showcase.\n2. 45-minute reading mentorship session where 
 mentors and students read together and do related activities aimed at 
 helping build literacy skills.\n\nTo learn more and register\, contact 
 duke@balletandbooks.org\n
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17325512
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17325512
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261031T173000Z
DTEND:20261031T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T000000Z
SUMMARY:Downtown Durham Chess Club
DESCRIPTION:\n\nParticipate in the Royal Game of Chess! \n\nThe Downtown 
 Durham Chess Club meets on selected Saturdays from 1:30-5:30 pm\; check the 
 calendar for dates.  All are welcome to attend regardless of age or skill 
 level. Instruction will be provided to beginners and novices. Sets and 
 boards are provided\, but you are welcome to bring your own if you wish.  
 Attendance is free.\n\nQuestions? Email wynnedavis@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4347\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Wynne Davis":MAILTO:wynnedavis@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Gaming
UID:LibCal-14288-17022969
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17022969
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261031T180000Z
DTEND:20261031T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T000000Z
SUMMARY:One Costume To Rule Them All!
DESCRIPTION:Step beyond the veil of Middle-earth and enter a realm of 
 legend at our Trick-or-Treating and Costume Contest!\n\nFrom the rolling 
 hills of the Shire to the fiery depths of Mordor\, we invite hobbits\, 
 elves\, dwarves\, wizards\, rangers\, and dark lords alike to bring their 
 favorite characters to life. Whether you channel the courage of Frodo 
 Baggins\, the wisdom of Gandalf\, the grace of Arwen\, or the power of 
 Aragorn\, this is your chance to step into the story and let your 
 imagination reign.\n\nParticipants will be judged on creativity and overall 
 presentation — so polish your armor\, practice your Elvish\, and don your 
 finest cloak. Everyone goes home with treats\, and the top two winners will 
 go home with their very own Funko POP! figurine. Let the journey begin! 
 Don't worry\, if Elves and Dwarves and Hobbits are not your thing\, you can 
 still participate and dress up as anything you want! \n\nPlease make sure 
 your costume is family-friendly and does not include any weapons!\n\nAll 
 ages are welcome! Registration is required. \n\nFor your presence\, you 
 will earn an extra entry into the One Walk to Rule Them All grand prize 
 drawing with submission of a completed tracker.\n\nThis program is made 
 possible through the generosity of the Friends of the Durham Library.
LOCATION:South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Friends of the Durham Library, One Walk, Other
UID:LibCal-14288-16219376
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16219376
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261031T180000Z
DTEND:20261031T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T000000Z
SUMMARY:Scary Stories To Tell In The Dark & Pumpkin Decorating
DESCRIPTION:The day has finally come! Halloween is here and we are 
 celebrating with a truly scary movie: Scary Stories To Tell In The Dark. 
 Based on the notorious children's book anthology\, this spooky movie is 
 actually quite scary and frightening. To help ease the nerves\, we will be 
 decorating mini-pumpkins alongside this terrifying flick! We like to keep 
 our supplies on the exact side of things\, so please register if you would 
 like a pumpkin to decorate! \n\n \n\nRated PG-13 for terrifying sequences\, 
 moderate violence & suggestive themes\n\nParents/Guardians\, please be 
 advised that this movie is more mature in content than what is typically 
 shown in our kids movie programs!
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Miles Simpson-Quigley":MAILTO:msquigley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17619969
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17619969
END:VEVENT
