SUMMARY:Computer Classes: Troubleshoot Your Tech
DESCRIPTION:Technology is meant to make our lives easier\, but it has bad 
 days\, too! Join us to learn more about what to do you when your devices 
 (smartphones\, tablets\, computers) won't work properly. We'll go over 
 basic troubleshooting steps\, as well as common issues including internet 
 connection\, slow performance\, keyboards and screens\, and more. Feel free 
 to bring your own device and any questions you may have!\n\nThis class is a 
 part of a series of computer classes. See the schedule below:\n\nMonday\, 
 September 28: AI Basics\nMonday\, October 12: Drop-In Tech Help\nMonday\, 
 October 19: Excel 101 \nMonday\, October 26: Drop-in Tech Help\nMonday\, 
 November 2: Troubleshoot Your Tech\nMonday\, November 9: Drop-in Tech 
 Help\nMonday\, November 16: Organize Your Photos\, Files\, & More
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Raivynn Smith":MAILTO:raivynnsmith@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Classes & Lectures, Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
